> Thanks, Chris. I like the idea of looking at the tau[position] parameters. I assume that, for seasonal home ranges, that value would ideally level off after a couple of days? I've been trying to use MSD plots to inform appropriate date cut-offs for seasonal residency, but there is still a lot of noise in the data. My dataset, and moose in general, are probably good tests if you are interested in non-stereotypical migratory behaviors. I've attached the some of our initial variograms (all seasons, all years) in case it helps.
